@exav/viewer: third-party notices
=================================

@exav/viewer is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). Its JavaScript
is exav's own, but for the wasm-bindgen glue in its modules. Its nine
WebAssembly modules are builds of exav-render, and its fonts are
third-party: this file gives their notices. The licence texts it refers to
are in LICENSES/, and in assets/fonts/ for the fonts.

The engines a host installs beside the package (pdfjs-dist, three,
@silurus/ooxml, @exav/unpack-wasm) are not part of its code, and carry their
own notices; the sandboxed frame app bundles them (Part 5).
`@exav/viewer/vite` and `exav-viewer-assets` copy some of pdf.js's files
into the host's build (CMaps, standard fonts, ICC profiles and ICC engine,
qcms): the host distributes those under their own licences, which
pdfjs-dist (Apache-2.0, qcms MIT) states. pdf.js's JPEG 2000 and JBIG2 decoders, builds of OpenJPEG and PDFium,
are not copied: wasm/openjpeg_nowasm_fallback.js and
wasm/jbig2_nowasm_fallback.js, this package's, take their place.


Part 1: in every WebAssembly module
====================================

wasm/exav_viewer_image_bg.wasm decodes raster images; wasm/exav_viewer_dwg_bg.wasm
reads DWG and DXF drawings and tessellates them; wasm/exav_viewer_model_bg.wasm
reads IFC and STL models and meshes them; wasm/exav_viewer_text_bg.wasm reads
Markdown into a tree; wasm/exav_viewer_sheets_bg.wasm converts XLS, ODS,
Numbers and other spreadsheets to XLSX (exav-render's office-sheets);
wasm/exav_viewer_slides_bg.wasm converts PPT, ODP, Keynote, ODG and VSDX
files to PPTX (exav-render's office-slides, with office-sheets for the charts
of ODP files); wasm/exav_viewer_docs_bg.wasm converts DOC, ODT, RTF, Word 2003
XML and Pages documents to DOCX (exav-render's office-docs). Two more
are embedded, in
base64, in the modules pdf.js imports in place of its own decoders:
exav_viewer_pdf_jpx_bg.wasm (JPXDecode) in wasm/openjpeg_nowasm_fallback.js,
exav_viewer_pdf_jbig2_bg.wasm (JBIG2Decode, CCITTFaxDecode) in
wasm/jbig2_nowasm_fallback.js.

exav-render, MIT, with, in the image module, source derivatives of image
0.25.9's JPEG and TIFF decoders and of tiff 0.10.3 (both MIT OR Apache-2.0,
used under the MIT License). Upstream: https://github.com/image-rs/image
(The image-rs Developers) and https://github.com/image-rs/image-tiff
(Copyright (c) 2018 PistonDevelopers). The DWG module also holds exav-unpack's
DXF and DWG readers, MIT.

Build-time crates (proc-macro2, quote, syn, unicode-ident, thiserror-impl,
fax_derive, multiversion_no_op, wasm-bindgen-macro,
wasm-bindgen-macro-support) generate code but do not reach the modules and
are not listed.


